nodecode-gmi-video is a rewrite of zkasuran's zkasuran/hermes-gmi-media:

  https://github.com/zkasuran/hermes-gmi-media
  commit 6760b29d6f9f93f47cef08702bda876fb10af652
  Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 zkasuran (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the original's GmiVideoProvider -- capabilities, model
selection and generate() -- is two tools and two verbs in this cell. The same
GMI request queue is spoken directly (GET models, GET models/<id>, POST
requests, GET requests/<id>) through the cell's own HTTP call, in place of the
original's httpx client; the live-schema mapping is carried over whole, so a
model's declared parameter names, option lists, nearest-value clamping, image
URL check, required-default fill, payload validation and dropped-option report
all behave as gmi_media.py does; the submit-and-poll loop keeps its backoff,
its 5xx retries, its terminal statuses and its deadline; the result download
keeps the HTTPS-only, no-bare-address check and the byte cap; the one-hour
model catalog keeps its TTL; and the price text, the interval price unit, the
request id and the scrubbed error text are the original's. The four
paragraphs it gave its picker are the (help :gmi-video) primer. The
GMI_API_KEY it read through Hermes secret scope is the gmi-video section's
api_key or api_key_env, with the environment variable still read, and the
Hermes video cache is the section's output_dir or the organism's cache.

What was left out, and why: the VideoGenProvider registration itself, and with
it register(), the capabilities() advertisement, get_setup_schema() and
list_models(), which a Hermes video picker read and a Nodecode has no lane
for -- the same data is gmi_video_models and the section's model and
image_model; the ThreadPoolExecutor catalog refresh, because one tool call
reads the catalog and there is no picker that must answer in 4.5 seconds; the
reference-image list, which the original also ignored and reported; and the
Hermes-only secrets scope and dotenv handling. LICENSE is the original
repository's LICENSE, unchanged.
